 V15 does not implement renew or another transition. The distinct seven-pin
 Stop, position-reserve witness, empirical capacity and dedicated production
 broker owner remain separate. Source stays in the private review candidate.
+
+## Forward V16: one renewed fence and seven-direct-pin original Stop
+
+This candidate extends the V15 closed laboratory with one recorder Renew
+at position four, after the exact committed Resume at three. It keeps the
+open mode, held scope/epoch and original fence ID, increments the revision
+from one to two, and creates one distinct operation identity and one new
+versioned fence fact. The old fence fact and its original identity remain.
+The actual recorder must own the active hold and supply the exact head,
+outer fence/revision and closed body. Both final-function and recognized
+COMMIT observations must fall before the old expiry. The new clock cannot
+precede the committed Resume observation. No changed broker or role grant
+is needed.
+
+Renew Result pins the previous fence digest and embeds the exact new record.
+The getter independently reconstructs both fence versions, including the
+old and new record digests and the closed new identity. Only the exact
+position-four fence record from that verified Renew may differ from its
+fence identity's allocation sequence. The general first-sequence
+association check remains for all other fact rows.
+
+Original reserved Stop from the renewed state uses the exact Resume Command
+as prior control and the exact Renew Command as prior head. It directly pins
+the renewed fence version without requiring current recorder authority or
+a live hold, clears the active fence and increments revision to three.
+Its historical closure includes both original fence versions. The previous
+paused and open Stop paths remain.
+
+The integrated native case expects seven direct pins and fourteen closure
+pins at Renew, followed by seven direct pins and seventeen closure pins
+at Stop. The five-operation witness expects 68 retained rows, 67 logical
+writes and 134 logical keys. It expects 72 row and 149 key touches including
+pending original inserts. It compares the selected Stop charge against the
+unchanged reserve. The structural proof continues to dominate the admitted
+Stop path and keeps the independent maximum previous-head Command cap.
+The remaining position-exhaustion and late Renew expiry witnesses need
+separate coverage.
+
+V16 retains all 34 accepted V15 IDs and adds one integrated native test.
+Only the unsupported-kind list changes among the prior method bodies.
+V15's measured 204.871 seconds leave limited headroom against the unchanged
+240-second run limit. V16 remains pending independent review and execution.
